## 💻 Python Code Standards
- **Follow PEP8** - Use 4 spaces for indentation, max 79 characters per line
- **Use type hints** - Always add type annotations to function parameters and return values
- **Docstrings** - Write comprehensive docstrings for all public functions and classes
- **Naming conventions** - snake_case for variables/functions, PascalCase for classes
- **Avoid magic numbers** - Define constants for any hardcoded values
- **Use context managers** - Prefer `with` statements for file operations and resource management

## 🔒 Security Rules
- **Never commit secrets** - Use environment variables for sensitive data
- **Validate inputs** - Always validate and sanitize user inputs
- **Use HTTPS** - All external API calls must use secure protocols
- **Log securely** - Never log sensitive information like passwords or tokens
- **Dependency scanning** - Regularly check for security vulnerabilities in dependencies

## 📊 Logging & Monitoring
- **Structured logging** - Use consistent log formats with proper levels (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR)
- **Context in logs** - Include request IDs, user IDs, and operation context in logs
- **Error handling** - Log errors with full stack traces for debugging
- **Performance monitoring** - Log operation timing and resource usage
- **Health checks** - Implement proper health check endpoints for services

## 🔧 Dependencies & Environment
- **Virtual environments** - Always use virtual environments (conda/venv)
- **Requirements files** - Keep requirements.txt, requirements-dev.txt, and requirements-vps.txt updated
- **Pin versions** - Pin dependency versions for reproducible builds
- **Minimal dependencies** - Only include necessary dependencies
- **Regular updates** - Regularly update dependencies for security and compatibility

## 📝 Documentation Rules
- **README updates** - Update README.md when adding new features or changing APIs
- **Code comments** - Comment complex business logic and algorithms
- **API documentation** - Document all public APIs with examples
- **Changelog** - Maintain a CHANGELOG.md for version releases
- **Inline docs** - Use # TODO and # FIXME comments for future improvements

## 🚀 Performance Guidelines
- **Async operations** - Use async/await for I/O operations
- **Database optimization** - Use proper indexing and query optimization
- **Caching** - Implement caching for expensive operations
- **Resource limits** - Set appropriate timeouts and resource limits
- **Memory management** - Be mindful of memory usage in long-running processes

## 🔄 Git & Version Control
- **Descriptive commits** - Write clear, descriptive commit messages
- **Branch naming** - Use feature/, bugfix/, hotfix/ prefixes for branches
- **PR descriptions** - Write detailed pull request descriptions
- **Squash merges** - Squash feature branches before merging to main
- **Pre-commit hooks** - Use pre-commit hooks for code quality checks

## 🏗️ Architecture Guidelines
- **Modular design** - Keep modules focused on single responsibilities
- **Dependency injection** - Use dependency injection for testability
- **Configuration management** - Externalize configuration from code
- **Error boundaries** - Implement proper error handling at service boundaries
- **API versioning** - Version APIs properly for backward compatibility
